      "text": "We are given the direction vectors for the line at $t=2$ and $t=3$ as $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}$\nand $\\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -4 \\end{pmatrix}.$  The difference between the two is \\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -4 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -8 \\end{pmatrix},\n\\] so the direction vector for the line at any other value of $t$ is \\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -8 \\end{pmatrix}  \\left( \\frac{t-2}{t-3} \\right) = \\begin{pmatrix} 2(t-2) \\\\ -8(t-2) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2t-4 \\\\ -8t + 16 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\] The vector on the line at $t = -7$ is then \\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} + \\begin{pmatrix} 2(-7)-4 \\\\ -8(-7) + 16 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} + \\begin{pmatrix} -18 \\\\ 76 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -17 \\\\ 80 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]",
